    "analysis": "Mrs. March directly avows her love for Jo, specifying Jo's effort to overcome shyness as a reason for that love. The utterance primarily presents an existing emotional state as true. It neither undertakes a relational commitment nor appears as a weakly propositional reflex or exclamation.",
