    "description": "Mrs. March addresses Jo directly in represented spoken dialogue: “I love you for it.”"
  },
  "contextual_interpretation": "Mrs. March warmly praises Jo for trying to fight her shyness and explicitly grounds her avowal in that effort. Her preceding encouragement and Jo's grateful thanks and kiss frame the utterance as sincere maternal affirmation. Its reassuring and approving functions remain contextual effects of a straightforward truth-conditional avowal rather than evidence of a new commitment."
  },
