      "evidence_id": "E1",
      "source": "local_text",
      "quotation_or_description": "“You do try to fight off your shyness, and I love you for it.”",
      "supports": "The first-person present-tense declaration explicitly presents the speaker's love for the addressee as an existing emotional state and gives a reason for it.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "E2",
      "source": "local_text",
      "quotation_or_description": "“Fighting faults isn’t easy, as I know, and a cheery word kind of gives a lift.”",
      "supports": "The surrounding reflective explanation makes the utterance deliberate encouragement rather than a predominantly reflex-like exclamation.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "E3",
      "source": "local_text",
      "quotation_or_description": "Jo responds, “Thank you, Mother,” and gives Mrs. March's cheek a grateful kiss.",
